    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0518" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg434"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    a copy and a translation into English of the reply of the German Government to
                    President Castro, which was sent to me in a memorandum from the Imperial foreign
                    office on the 6th of January, 1903.</p>
                <p>Immediately upon receipt of this memorandum I communicated it to you in a
                    telegram.</p>
                <p>I received on the 6th of January your telegram announcing the fact that you had
                    then received the reply of Great Britain which appointed the British ambassador
                    in Washington to treat with Mr. Bowen.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne
                    Tower.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d401-a1.xml" xpointer="d401-a1"/>
            </div>
